 "about_text": "The Tolman Collection is a Tokyo gallery specializing in contemporary Japanese prints, founded in 1972 by Norman and Mary Tolman. Often described as Japan's oldest foreign-owned gallery devoted to contemporary Japanese printmaking, it has built decades-long relationships with print artists, publishing exclusive editions and maintaining extensive archives. The gallery represents nearly fifty artists, working directly with them to ensure provenance and quality. Leadership passed to second-generation owner Allison Tolman, with Daisuke Maruoka serving as President. In addition to its Tokyo gallery, the collection operates a branch in New York. Over five decades it has organized exhibitions at institutions worldwide, including Zojoji Temple, the Singapore Art Museum, the Cairo Opera House, and Finland's Retretti Art Centre, helping introduce Japanese graphic art to international audiences.",
